  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CommAddDisc 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "At a patient advisory board meeting, a research team updates the community
    on ongoing discovery work. They mention that they are collecting donated patient
    blood samples to test how new drug compounds work on cancer cells. You want to
    ask how these samples will be used and how the donors\u2019 wishes are respected,
    but the discussion has quickly become science-focused \u2014 and community advocates
    have no role in ethical considerations until human trials begin, anyway.\n\nIs
    this true or false?"
  explanation: "Community advocates can highlight ethical considerations even before
    trials start, such as how donated samples are handled and how research is communicated.
    Their involvement helps ensure research stays patient-centered and ethically
    responsible from the very beginning. By speaking up about patients\u2019 rights
    and preferences early on, advocates help build trust and transparency between
    the research team and the community."
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Community Advocate
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
